":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-1.5}],"uuid":"c84c6ad9-6efc-5708-8dc6-b10f18bb9010","time":1.95,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"2f8cc36c-ddd2-5997-9f6d-1a42c4b7cd58","time":2.2,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"934d7f7d-9ef9-5820-ae83-52635c30eb08","time":2.5,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"}]},"91572a96-9c29-5a53-b2a9-8c340b5ecf24":{"name":"canopy_2","type":"bone","keyframes":[{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"a5629178-e3ca-5715-90ed-3db5741a5ac5","time":0,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"7c694970-6414-536f-ac2c-fe987335373e","time":1.45,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-4.0}],"uuid":"cda4d51c-36b9-5e94-a946-e3af4f035be5","time":1.55,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":3.0}],"uuid":"615eb766-deff-5c72-b6a1-ebf4a04157de","time":1.75,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-1.5}],"uuid":"7a51f7ad-d4da-52d3-b3fa-4a4d7834868e","time":1.95,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"71924e12-cc57-5576-896d-5c27e5757605","time":2.2,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"},{"channel":"rotation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"8ebdd4d7-2cea-5bbb-9137-29f006c33213","time":2.5,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"}]}}}],"description":"# tree_oak_great\n\nReference great oak of the Deepwoods: a massive trunk about 1.5 m across, huge spreading limbs, about 21 m (747 u). Deep bark grooves, moss, a hollow: old and important.\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -320..330, y 0..730, z -315..320 units (18.28 x 20.53 x 17.86 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 512 x 256 tile atlas, 1 px per unit, faces cut to fit (FALLBACK because tree_oak_great: 94 face regions, 1400314 px, do not fit 1024 x 1024).\n- Cubes: 125.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- trunk: 53 x 747 x 53 at the origin (the solid, blocking part)\n- canopy: see bounds; units walk under it\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `rustle` | 5.0 | loop | canopy bones sway very slightly (trunk still) |\n| `hit` | 0.4 | once | canopy shivers after an axe strike |\n| `fall` | 2.5 | once | whole `tree` group tips over sideways onto +X about the trunk base edge, hits at 1.5 s, bounces once, settles by 2.1 s; canopy whips on impact |\n\n## Notes\n\n- `rustle` and `hit` move only the canopy groups; `fall` rotates the `tree` group (pivot on the trunk base edge on +X), so the trunk lies along +X after 1.5 s (it stops short of flat where the crown meets the ground). Swap to the `_stump` model (and spawn the `_log_pile`) once it has settled.\n- Protected by the Elves. The hollow faces -Z at the base (dark recess, 24 x 50 u). Moss on the west side and a mossy step on the root flare.\n"}